     <h1>Fender Jazzmaster</h1>

     <img src="Images/Leo.jpg" width="250" alt="Leo Fender - Inventor of the Jazzmaster">

     <h2>About the Jazzmaster</h2>
     <p>
         The Fender Jazzmaster is one of the most iconic electric guitars ever made. 
         It is known for its warm, mellow tone, unique offset body, and sophisticated electronics, making it a favorite among indie, surf, and alternative rock guitarists.
     </p>

     <h2>History</h2>
     <p>
         The Jazzmaster was introduced by Leo Fender in 1958 as Fender's top-of-the-line model. 
         Although originally designed to appeal to jazz guitarists with its rich hum-canceling-like pickups, it later found its true home in the 1960s surf rock scene and the 1980s/90s alternative and indie rock movements.
     </p>

     <h2>Common Uses</h2>
     <p>The Fender Jazzmaster is especially known for:</p>
     <ul>
         <li>Alternative rock, indie, and shoegaze music</li>
         <li>Surf rock and retro instrumental music</li>
         <li>Atmospheric, ambient tones with heavy effects (reverb/delay)</li>
         <li>Expressive tremolo arm (whammy bar) usage</li>
         <li>Warm, smooth neck pickup tones</li>
     </ul>

     <h2>Famous Players</h2>
     <p>
         Many legendary guitarists have used the Jazzmaster, including J Mascis (Dinosaur Jr.), Kevin Shields (My Bloody Valentine), and Elvis Costello.
     </p>

